    "created_at": "2026-06-02T09:17:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-02T09:17:20Z",
    "body": "Why would that depend on `appearance: auto`? You'd also need that when the `button` element is not used, presumably. We should not make tree mutations depend on the `appearance` value.\n\nI also think the question posed above is wrong, as whether the `select` element button text reacts to mutations is not a function of its `appearance` value, its a function of its structure in the node tree. If you use a `button` element it's only synchronized at select points in time. If you don't use a `button` element it's live. And yes, if you want to mimic liveness with the `button` element you'd have to listen to mutations yourself (or ensure you drive all mutations and can make them in multiple places).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
